From: Timur Ravilov <93673987+t0b1kent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 01:57:53 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 43/46] EXPERIMENT: constrain PE32 FIP tracking to x87 decoder
 tables

Family: decoder-table identity for x87 metadata, versus overlapping raw opcode bytes.
Members: X87F80Ops and X87F64Ops; all foreign tables excluded. Trigger siblings: SSE66 0F D8..DF, sharing raw D8..DF with primary x87 escapes.
Evidence: Frontend NormalOpHeader assigns secondary opcode to OPRaw; NormalOp supplies actual TableInfo. Imported raw-byte-only gate tracked SSE as x87 and changed saved FIP.
Correction: after the existing default-OFF MACRUNNER_HB_X87_FIX_FIP_CS32 gate, require TableInfo within either x87 array. No new guest ABI or runtime stores.
Regression: all eight SSE D8..DF witnesses strict NEW before -> EQUAL8/8 after. Final shifted matrix retains EQUAL43 plus two unchanged CALL faults of our old native address adapter. Pop control KNOWN9, sticky control KNOWN2, env control KNOWN16; zero-restore siblings52/52 EQUAL. Full80 tested; reduced64 table eligibility implemented but numerical acceptance NOT_ENABLED. Original two-base/game and ASM64 acceptance still incomplete; no product install, no GOAL.
Cost: this eligibility check runs during IR generation. Correction costs already measured on the prior fipcs runner, SHA1f44438238cc96f1eeb69c2e490c0e2ed567f6caf24fa0ba444607de8eaaec8c; no universal latency or final-byte golden claim.
Audit completed: yes for table identity batch; metadata FOP/FDP/DS/FXSAVE remains separate documented scope.
---
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/X87.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/X87.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/X87.cpp
index 452b816ab..332a0e2e0 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/X87.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/X87.cpp
@@ -340,6 +340,15 @@ void OpDispatchBuilder::TrackX87Instruction32(OpcodeArgs) {
   if (!FEXCore::HBX87::StateFix::InstructionPointers32()) {
     return;
   }
+  // Secondary/SSE tables reuse raw D8..DF bytes. They must not change FIP.
+  // Decoder table identity also covers the reduced-precision x87 table.
+  const auto Table = reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(Op->TableInfo);
+  const auto Full = reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(FEXCore::X86Tables::X87F80Ops.data());
+  const auto Reduced = reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(FEXCore::X86Tables::X87F64Ops.data());
+  if (!((Table >= Full && Table < Full + sizeof(FEXCore::X86Tables::X87F80Ops)) ||
+        (Table >= Reduced && Table < Reduced + sizeof(FEXCore::X86Tables::X87F64Ops)))) {
+    return;
+  }
   // Imported from GUEST32-BASE 386457d86cf32d34: control instructions
   // preserve the last computational x87 instruction in protected mode.
   const uint8_t Escape = Op->OPRaw;
